# TLE987x firmware style

- Language: C99 (Keil ARM Compiler 5/6 or project-selected toolchain).
- Keep ISRs short; defer heavy work to main/loop or flags.
- Init order: clocks/PMU → GPIO → peripherals → interrupts → motor enable last.
- Use Config Wizard–generated `*_conf.h` / init where the project already does; do not hand-edit generated blocks without matching the wizard XML.
- Prefer SDK helpers (`CCU6_*`, `BDRV_*`, `ADC*_*`, `LIN_*`) over magic numbers.
- Guard motor enable behind fault clears (OC, UV, overtemp) when BDRV/CSA are used.
- Avoid dynamic allocation; static/`const` in flash when possible.
- Comment placeholders for board pin mux when eval-kit vs custom PCB differs.

```c
// ❌ BAD — enable bridge before faults/PWM are safe
BDRV_Set_Bridge(Chrg_Pump_En, Bridge_On);

// ✅ GOOD — PWM/dead-time + fault path ready, then enable
CCU6_StartTmr_T12();
/* clear latched faults, then */
BDRV_Set_Bridge(Chrg_Pump_En, Bridge_On);
```
